{
  "id": 6,
  "title": "Home & everyday objects",
  "goal": "Name rooms and household objects, say where things are, and say what there is (and isn't) in a place.",
  "intro": "English uses prepositions *before* a noun (in the room); Telugu uses **case suffixes and postpositions after** it: *గదిలో* (gadilō, room-in), *బల్ల మీద* (balla mīda, table on).\n\nSome nouns change shape before these endings. The most important is *ఇల్లు* (house), which becomes *ఇంటి-*: *ఇంట్లో* (at home), *ఇంటి దగ్గర* (near the house).",
